{
  "spec": "exec protocol v1.4 sandbox job notify (crates/agent/src/exec_endpoint.rs, \"Sandbox job notify (v1.4)\"), \"The callback request\" and \"The receiver\"",
  "notes": [
    "requests: what an endpoint sends for a job kept with notify. body is the exact bytes; headers lists every header the endpoint must send (others the HTTP client adds, such as Host and Content-Length, are not listed, and a Cookie header is forbidden).",
    "receiver: one request to /_beyond/agent?session_id=<grant.session_id>&keep=<generation>. request.grant is the session grant the edge attached for grant.tenant and grant.session_id: callback (it carries \"purpose\": \"job_ended\"), user (an ordinary grant), or failing (one that does not verify at this replica). request.authorization lists the request's Authorization header values, in order (empty: none). state is what the replica holds: notify_key (it holds the verifier keys of v1.4-token.json), session_exists (the session is in storage), job (released: the session tracks it released and the sandbox still runs it; ended_unreported: the sandbox has it ended and the ledger does not mark its end reported; held: the session holds its stream and the callback is not its proof; end_reported: the ledger marks its end reported; no_record: the transcript's ledger has no record of it), reconcile (ok, or fails: the sandbox cannot be listed), run_in_flight (a run holds the session). expect: the HTTP status, whether the session may be opened or reached, and whether anything is sent to the sandbox.",
    "edge: how the edge classifies a request by its Authorization header values (E1, with the rules of N30): callback (forwarded with a callback grant), user (handled as any user request), or refused with status, never forwarded."
  ],
  "keep": {
    "scope": "2ff302a37e7401aa95f92ec6c431944a",
    "id": "0123456789abcdef",
    "url": "https://edge.example/_beyond/agent?session_id=a07-s3.01J9ZQ4N6V&keep=5be0c2a19f3d7e41",
